# .gitattributes — Maldros analytics system
#
# Added Session 110 (P-146).
#
# Until now the .pptx and .pdf under case-study/ survived on git's binary
# detection heuristic alone. A heuristic is not a rule. A compressed container
# git guesses wrong about gets line-ending conversion applied to its bytes,
# which corrupts it silently — and the corruption is invisible to every text
# search, exactly like the Session 108 term that shipped inside the deck.
#
# Scope is deliberately limited to binary declarations, matching the queued
# task. Full text/EOL normalisation (`* text=auto eol=lf`) is NOT set here: it
# would renormalise the entire tree in a single commit immediately before a
# publication flip. That is a separate decision, not a side effect of this one.

# --- Office containers and PDFs ---------------------------------------------
*.pptx      binary
*.potx      binary
*.docx      binary
*.dotx      binary
*.xlsx      binary
*.xlsm      binary
*.pdf       binary

# --- Columnar data ----------------------------------------------------------
# Not currently tracked. Declared ahead of the BigQuery/DuckDB migration path,
# where Parquet is the interchange format.
*.parquet   binary
*.db        binary
*.sqlite    binary

# --- Images -----------------------------------------------------------------
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.gif       binary
*.ico       binary
*.webp      binary

# --- Archives and fonts -----------------------------------------------------
*.zip       binary
*.woff      binary
*.woff2     binary
*.ttf       binary
*.otf       binary
*.eot       binary
